---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Nile FAQ: Hosting, Tickets, Watching & Advertising";
const description =
  "Answers on streaming equipment, ticket pricing, payouts, replays, watching without an app, and advertising on Nile.";

const sections = [
  {
    id: "hosts",
    label: "For hosts",
    descriptor: "Going live & getting paid",
    items: [
      {
        q: "What equipment do I need to stream?",
        a: "Just phones. Mount two or more phones at different angles and you have a Nile show. There's no minimum equipment requirement beyond that. A crew of two friends handling the phones is all it takes to get started.",
      },
      {
        q: "How does pricing work? Where does my money go?",
        a: "You set the ticket price. Paid shows start at $3 for the first hour, plus $1 for each extra half hour. You keep 60% of every ticket and replay sold, and card fees come out of Nile's share, not yours. Tips are yours minus a 10% fee. Payouts go through Stripe directly to your account.",
      },
      {
        q: "Can I offer a free event?",
        a: "Yes. Free shows can run up to two hours and stream in standard definition, and they aren't recorded, so there's no replay afterward. Live multi-angle streaming has real costs, and those limits are how free shows stay possible. When you want HD, longer shows and a replay to sell, make it a paid show.",
      },
      {
        q: "What if nobody buys a ticket?",
        a: "That's a real risk worth thinking about before you go live. The best way to avoid it is to build anticipation before the show: announce early, share your event link, and give your audience a reason to tune in. Nile gives you a ticketed experience worth promoting. The promotion is still on you.",
      },
      {
        q: "What camera angles can I stream?",
        a: "As many as you have phones for. Each phone in your setup becomes a separate angle that your audience can switch between. A two-phone setup gives you two angles. Add more phones, get more angles.",
      },
      {
        q: "What happens if my stream drops mid-show?",
        a: "You can rejoin the stream without ending the show. The broadcast keeps running, and your audience stays in the session. A dropped connection doesn't mean a cancelled event.",
      },
      {
        q: "Can I premiere a pre-recorded film on Nile?",
        a: "Yes. Upload your film ahead of time from the Film screen in the Nile app (up to 8 hours and 30 GB; a computer is best for big files), along with an optional trailer, poster and captions. At the start time you introduce it on camera and press Play, and everyone watches in step. When the credits roll, your cast joins you on stage for a live Q&A. You choose whether chat stays open during the film and whether there's a replay, and for how long.",
      },
      {
        q: "Who owns my film if I premiere it on Nile?",
        a: "You do. Nile is a platform for selling access to your event, not a distributor. We don't take ownership of your work, we don't claim exclusivity, and we don't acquire rights to it. You're licensing us to stream it for your event and to host the replay you choose to sell.",
      },
      {
        q: "Does premiering on Nile affect my festival or distribution options?",
        a: "That depends on the festival or distributor, not on us. Many festivals have premiere-status rules that count any public screening, online included. Check the rules for the festivals you're targeting before you set a date. If your film is already through its festival run, or you're skipping it, a Nile premiere is yours to schedule whenever you want.",
      },
      {
        q: "How does VOD work?",
        a: "Every paid show records a replay automatically. Live ticket buyers watch it at no extra charge. After the show you set a replay price for everyone else (or make it free); if you don't, it goes up at your ticket price after 48 hours. Replays stay available for 30 days, and replay sales pay out the same way as tickets.",
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: "viewers",
    label: "For fans",
    descriptor: "Watching & tickets",
    items: [
      {
        q: "Do viewers need to download an app?",
        a: "No. Viewers can watch any Nile event from a web browser without downloading anything. The Nile app is available for iOS and Android and offers the full experience, but it's not required.",
      },
      {
        q: "Missed the show. Can I still watch?",
        a: "Usually. Paid shows have an on-demand replay for 30 days after the show, and if you bought a live ticket you already have access. Free shows are live only. Check the event page to see whether a replay is available and what it costs.",
      },
      {
        q: "How do I find events to watch?",
        a: "Download the Nile app and follow the creators, artists, or communities you care about. You'll be notified when they go live or post a new event. You can also browse upcoming events in the Discover tab.",
      },
      {
        q: "What shows up in my feed?",
        a: "Only what you asked for. When you sign up, you pick the topics you care about, and that's all Nile shows you. There's no hidden algorithm surfacing content you didn't choose. If your interests change, open Settings at any time and update your topics.",
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: "advertisers",
    label: "For advertisers",
    descriptor: "Reaching the audience",
    items: [
      {
        q: "How do I get started advertising on Nile?",
        a: "Through the self-serve ad portal at ads.joinnile.com. Pick a format, upload your creative, choose the topics you want to reach and a budget from $10, and launch. Every ad is checked against our ad policies before it runs. No sales call, no contract, no agency required.",
      },
      {
        q: "What ad formats are available?",
        a: "Three: feed ads (an image card in the home feed), Currents ads (a vertical video of up to 60 seconds between Currents), and event sponsorships, where you make an offer to sponsor a specific show's pre-show lobby. The host decides whether to accept, you're only charged if they do, and they can put your logo on screen during the show too. All three run from the same self-serve portal.",
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: "general",
    label: "General",
    descriptor: "Everything else",
    items: [
      {
        q: "Is Nile available in my country?",
        a: "Nile is available globally for viewers. Host availability and payout support depend on Stripe's coverage in your region. Check Stripe's supported countries list to confirm payouts are available where you are.",
      },
    ],
  },
];

// Structured data for search, built from the same list so the two can't drift.
const faqSchema = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: sections.flatMap((sec) =>
    sec.items.map((i) => ({
      "@type": "Question",
      name: i.q,
      acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: i.a },
    })),
  ),
});
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical="/faq">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqSchema} />
  </Fragment>

  <!-- PAGE HEADER -->
  <section class="page-header nile-section">
    <div class="nile-container header-inner">
      <p class="nile-eyebrow">FAQ</p>
      <h1>Questions? We've got answers.</h1>
      <p class="header-sub">
        Everything you need to know about going live, watching, and advertising
        on Nile.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ CONTENT -->
  <section class="faq-body nile-section">
    <div class="nile-container faq-sections">
      {
        sections.map((s, si) => (
          <section id={s.id} class="faq-section">
            <h2 class="section-label">
              {s.label}
              <span class="section-descriptor">{s.descriptor}</span>
            </h2>
            <div class="faq-items">
              {s.items.map((item, ii) => (
                <details class="faq-item" open={si === 0 && ii === 0}>
                  <summary class="faq-q">
                    <span>{item.q}</span>
                    <span class="faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true" />
                  </summary>
                  <p class="faq-a">{item.a}</p>
                </details>
              ))}
            </div>
          </section>
        ))
      }

      <!-- Still have questions -->
      <div class="still-questions nile-card">
        <p class="sq-label">Still have questions?</p>
        <p>
          Contact us at <a href="mailto:support@joinnile.com" class="email-link"
            >support@joinnile.com</a
          > and we'll get back to you.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Header sits on page-black (section 1). Generous bottom padding gives the
     hero its own breathing room before the tinted FAQ band below. */
  .page-header {
    padding-block: var(--nile-s-16) var(--nile-s-12);
  }
  .header-inner {
    max-width: 760px;
  }
  .header-inner h1 {
    margin-bottom: var(--nile-s-6);
  }
  .header-sub {
    color: var(--nile-txt-secondary);
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    max-width: 540px;
  }

  /* Layout — single centered column. FAQ body is section 2, so it takes the
     automatic surface tint from brand.css. Standard section top padding gives
     the first "For hosts" heading clean clearance from the band's top edge. */
  .faq-body {
    padding-block: var(--nile-s-16);
  }
  .faq-sections {
    max-width: 920px;
  }

  /* Section headings */
  .faq-section {
    margin-bottom: var(--nile-s-10);
  }
  .section-label {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--nile-s-3);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    font-family: var(--nile-font-display);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--nile-txt-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--nile-s-4);
  }
  .section-descriptor {
    font-family: var(--nile-font-body);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--nile-txt-tertiary);
  }

  /* FAQ items — one rounded card per group */
  .faq-items {
    border: 1px solid var(--nile-border);
    border-radius: var(--nile-r-lg);
    background: var(--nile-bg-raised);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .faq-item {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--nile-border);
    border-left: 2px solid transparent;
    transition: background 0.15s, border-color 0.15s;
  }
  .faq-item:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }
  .faq-item[open] {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--nile-volt) 7%, var(--nile-bg-raised));
    border-left-color: var(--nile-volt);
  }
  .faq-q {
    padding: var(--nile-s-5) var(--nile-s-6);
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--nile-s-4);
    color: var(--nile-txt-primary);
    transition: color 0.15s;
  }
  .faq-q::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  .faq-item[open] .faq-q {
    color: var(--nile-volt);
  }

  /* Circular +/- toggle */
  .faq-toggle {
    position: relative;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 32px;
    height: 32px;
    border-radius: var(--nile-r-pill);
    border: 1px solid var(--nile-border);
    background: var(--nile-bg-surface);
    transition: background 0.15s, border-color 0.15s;
  }
  /* horizontal bar (always) */
  .faq-toggle::before,
  .faq-toggle::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    width: 12px;
    height: 2px;
    background: var(--nile-txt-secondary);
    border-radius: 2px;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    transition: opacity 0.2s, background 0.15s;
  }
  /* vertical bar — hidden when open to make a minus */
  .faq-toggle::after {
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%) rotate(90deg);
  }
  .faq-item[open] .faq-toggle {
    background: var(--nile-volt);
    border-color: var(--nile-volt);
  }
  .faq-item[open] .faq-toggle::before {
    background: var(--nile-bg-page);
  }
  .faq-item[open] .faq-toggle::after {
    opacity: 0;
  }

  .faq-a {
    color: var(--nile-txt-secondary);
    padding: 0 var(--nile-s-6) var(--nile-s-5);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: 70ch;
  }

  /* Still have questions */
  .still-questions {
    margin-top: var(--nile-s-6);
  }
  .sq-label {
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: var(--nile-s-2);
  }
  .still-questions p:last-child {
    color: var(--nile-txt-secondary);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .email-link {
    color: var(--nile-volt);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .faq-q {
      padding: var(--nile-s-4);
      font-size: 1rem;
    }
    .faq-a {
      padding: 0 var(--nile-s-4) var(--nile-s-4);
    }
  }
</style>
